eggp: bad value for -N
eggp: 
eggp: Usage: <prog> <args> [+RTS <rtsopts> | -RTS <args>] ... --RTS <args>
eggp: 
eggp:    +RTS     Indicates run time system options follow
eggp:    -RTS     Indicates program arguments follow
eggp:   --RTS     Indicates that ALL subsequent arguments will be given to the
eggp:             program (including any of these RTS flags)
eggp: 
eggp: The following run time system options may be available (note that some
eggp: of these may not be usable unless this program was linked with the -rtsopts
eggp: flag):
eggp: 
eggp:   -?        Prints this message and exits; the program is not executed
eggp:   --info    Print information about the RTS used by this program
eggp: 
eggp:   --nonmoving-gc
eggp:             Selects the non-moving mark-and-sweep garbage collector to
eggp:             manage the oldest generation.
eggp:   --copying-gc
eggp:             Selects the copying garbage collector to manage all generations.
eggp: 
eggp:   -K<size>  Sets the maximum stack size (default: 80% of the heap)
eggp:             e.g.: -K32k -K512k -K8M
eggp:   -ki<size> Sets the initial thread stack size (default 1k)  e.g.: -ki4k -ki2m
eggp:   -kc<size> Sets the stack chunk size (default 32k)
eggp:   -kb<size> Sets the stack chunk buffer size (default 1k)
eggp: 
eggp:   -A<size>  Sets the minimum allocation area size (default 4m) e.g.: -A20m -A10k
eggp:   -AL<size> Sets the amount of large-object memory that can be allocated
eggp:             before a GC is triggered (default: the value of -A)
eggp:   -F<n>     Sets the collecting threshold for old generations as a factor of
eggp:             the live data in that generation the last time it was collected
eggp:             (default: 2.0)
eggp:   -Fd<n>    Sets the inverse rate which memory is returned to the OS after being
eggp:             optimistically retained after being allocated. Subsequent major
eggp:             collections not caused by heap overflow will return an amount of
eggp:             memory controlled by this factor (higher is slower). Setting the factor
eggp:             to 0 means memory is not returned.
eggp:             (default 4.0)
eggp:   -n<size>  Allocation area chunk size (0 = disabled, default: 0)
eggp:   -O<size>  Sets the minimum size of the old generation (default 1M)
eggp:   -M<size>  Sets the maximum heap size (default unlimited)  e.g.: -M256k -M1G
eggp:   -H<size>  Sets the minimum heap size (default 0M)   e.g.: -H24m  -H1G
eggp:   -xb<addr> Sets the address from which a suitable start for the heap memory
eggp:             will be searched from. This is useful if the default address
eggp:             clashes with some third-party library.
eggp:   -xn       Use the non-moving collector for the old generation.
eggp:   -m<n>     Minimum % of heap which must be available (default 3%)
eggp:   -G<n>     Number of generations (default: 2)
eggp:   -c<n>     Use in-place compaction instead of copying in the oldest generation
eggp:             when live data is at least <n>% of the maximum heap size set with
eggp:             -M (default: 30%)
eggp:   -c        Use in-place compaction for all oldest generation collections
eggp:             (the default is to use copying)
eggp:   -w        Use mark-region for the oldest generation (experimental)
eggp:   -I<sec>   Perform full GC after <sec> idle time (default: 0.3, 0 == off)
eggp:   -Iw<sec>  Minimum wait time between idle GC runs (default: 0, 0 == no min wait time)
eggp: 
eggp:   -T         Collect GC statistics (useful for in-program statistics access)
eggp:   -t[<file>] One-line GC statistics (if <file> omitted, uses stderr)
eggp:   -s[<file>] Summary  GC statistics (if <file> omitted, uses stderr)
eggp:   -S[<file>] Detailed GC statistics (if <file> omitted, uses stderr)
eggp: 
eggp: 
eggp:   -Z         Don't squeeze out update frames on context switch
eggp:   -B         Sound the bell at the start of each garbage collection
eggp:   -h       Heap residency profile (output file <program>.hp)
eggp:   -hT      Produce a heap profile grouped by closure type
eggp:   -hi      Produce a heap profile grouped by info table address
eggp:   -po<file>  Override profiling output file name prefix (program name by default)
eggp:   -i<sec>  Time between heap profile samples (seconds, default: 0.1)
eggp:   --no-automatic-heap-samples
eggp:            Do not start the heap profile interval timer on start-up,
eggp:            Rather, the application will be responsible for triggering
eggp:            heap profiler samples.
eggp:   -ol<file>  Send binary eventlog to <file> (default: <program>.eventlog)
eggp:   -l[flags]  Log events to a file
eggp:              where [flags] can contain:
eggp:                 s    scheduler events
eggp:                 g    GC and heap events
eggp:                 n    non-moving GC heap census events
eggp:                 p    par spark events (sampled)
eggp:                 f    par spark events (full detail)
eggp:                 u    user events (emitted from Haskell code)
eggp:                 a    all event classes above
eggp:                -x    disable an event class, for any flag above
eggp:              the initial enabled event classes are 'sgpu'
eggp:  --eventlog-flush-interval=<secs>
eggp:              Periodically flush the eventlog at the specified interval.
eggp: 
eggp:   -C<secs>  Context-switch interval in seconds.
eggp:             0 or no argument means switch as often as possible.
eggp:             Default: 0.02 sec.
eggp:   -V<secs>  Master tick interval in seconds (0 == disable timer).
eggp:             This sets the resolution for -C and the heap profile timer -i,
eggp:             and is the frequency of time profile samples.
eggp:             Default: 0.01 sec.
eggp: 
eggp:   -N[<n>]    Use <n> processors (default: 1, -N alone determines
eggp:              the number of processors to use automatically)
eggp:   -maxN[<n>] Use up to <n> processors automatically
eggp:   -qg[<n>]   Use parallel GC only for generations >= <n>
eggp:              (default: 0, -qg alone turns off parallel GC)
eggp:   -qb[<n>]   Use load-balancing in the parallel GC only for generations >= <n>
eggp:              (default: 1 for -A < 32M, 0 otherwise;
eggp:               -qb alone turns off load-balancing)
eggp:   -qn<n>     Use <n> threads for parallel GC (defaults to value of -N)
eggp:   -qa        Use the OS to set thread affinity (experimental)
eggp:   -qm        Don't automatically migrate threads between CPUs
eggp:   -qi<n>     If a processor has been idle for the last <n> GCs, do not
eggp:              wake it up for a non-load-balancing parallel GC.
eggp:              (0 disables,  default: 0)
eggp:   --numa[=<node_mask>]
eggp:              Use NUMA, nodes given by <node_mask> (default: off)
eggp:   --install-signal-handlers=<yes|no>
eggp:              Install signal handlers (default: yes)
eggp:   --io-manager=<name>
eggp:              The I/O manager to use.
eggp:              Options available: auto mio (default: mio)
eggp:   -e<n>      Maximum number of outstanding local sparks (default: 4096)
eggp:   -xp        Assume that all object files were compiled with -fPIC
eggp:              -fexternal-dynamic-refs and load them anywhere in the address
eggp:              space
eggp:   -xm        Base address to mmap memory in the GHCi linker
eggp:              (hex; must be <80000000)
eggp:   -xq        The allocation limit given to a thread after it receives
eggp:              an AllocationLimitExceeded exception. (default: 100k)
eggp: 
eggp:   -xr        The size of virtual memory address space reserved by the
eggp:              two step allocator (default: 1T)
eggp: 
eggp:   -Mgrace=<n>
eggp:              The amount of allocation after the program receives a
eggp:              HeapOverflow exception before the exception is thrown again, if
eggp:              the program is still exceeding the heap limit.
eggp: 
eggp:   --read-tix-file=<yes|no>
eggp:              Whether to initialize HPC datastructures from  <program>.tix              at the start of execution. (default: yes)
eggp: 
eggp:   --write-tix-file=<yes|no>
eggp:              Whether to write <program>.tix at the end of execution.
eggp:              (default: yes)
